<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?> <!-- Declare XML version and text encoding so Visual Studio and MSBuild can read the elements below. Angle syntax: The < and > bound the XML declaration; the question marks mark it as declaration syntax specifying how the following file is decoded. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
<Project ToolsVersion="Current" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003"> <!-- Define per-user Visual Studio project settings, separate from the shared compiler and source configuration. Angle syntax: The < and > bound the opening Project tag; attributes describe this element, and its child elements continue until the matching closing tag below. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
  <PropertyGroup /> <!-- Keep per-user properties empty; the shared project supplies its build settings. Angle syntax: The < and > bound a self-closing PropertyGroup element; the slash means this single line supplies the element without a separate closing tag. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
</Project> <!-- Close Project; following elements return to its parent. Angle syntax: The < and > bound a closing Project tag, and the slash identifies the end of the matching group opened above. The angle symbols at the comment boundaries enclose this explanation as XML commentary, which the application and build tools ignore. -->
